WEBVTT

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:09.940
Labor: A robot specifically designed
for construction work.

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:12.820
Labors allow dramatic advances
in construction...

00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:14.660
but also in crime.

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:16.780
To combat these
new Labor crimes...

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:20.490
the police created a special unit:
The Patrol Labor.

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:24.260
And thus, the birth of Patlabor.

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:49.860
moshimo ima anata no yume no eria ga
Should the area of your dreams

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:55.250
namida ni okasare
Be invaded now by tears

00:00:55.990 --> 00:01:01.990
kujiketa toki wa nee kokoro de
When I faltered, in my heart

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:08.330
watashi no namae yonde
My name calls

00:01:08.330 --> 00:01:13.170
hurry up hurry up ai no tsubasa
Hurry up, hurry up, the wings of love

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:20.180
anata no sora e tonde yuku
Will fly to your sky

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:24.430
I’m gonna fly fly away

00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:27.440
KONDISHON GUURIN
Condition green

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:33.530
mukai kanashimi wo tasuketai no
Do you want to help this deep sorrow?

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:36.530
Just fly fly away

00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:42.740
onaji itami wo mune no REDAA wa
The radar of your heart

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:49.050
itsu demo kanjite iru wa
Is always feeling the same pain

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:55.390
Just I'm gonna fly away

00:01:57.340 --> 00:02:01.650
The Working Girl

00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:20.910
Stay back!

00:02:21.910 --> 00:02:23.490
If you care about her...

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:24.710
Momoko!

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:27.170
Excuse me.

00:02:27.330 --> 00:02:28.960
Attention criminal.

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:32.010
Be careful not to kill your hostage.

00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:35.220
I'll take her with me to <i>hell!</i>

00:02:37.210 --> 00:02:39.300
But it's such a beautiful day.

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:44.260
Life isn't that bad, you know.
Let's talk this over.

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:46.310
Enough talk!

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:48.780
Momoko!

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:57.160
Dear viewers:
I don't think I'll last much longer.

00:02:57.740 --> 00:02:59.790
I'm glad you let me into your homes.

00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:04.420
I was... truly happy.

00:03:09.410 --> 00:03:12.380
The tape is rolling. In ten seconds...

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:16.050
Five,

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:16.930
four,

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:17.930
three,

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:27.650
Welcome back, viewers.
This episode of <i>The Working Girl</i>,

00:03:28.390 --> 00:03:33.520
comes from Landfill 13,
home of the police Special Vehicles team,

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:36.280
better known as Patlabor!

00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:43.110
Division 2 has disastrous nicknames:

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:44.660
Unwanted Baggage,

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:47.460
and Specialists in Destructive Justice.

00:03:47.530 --> 00:03:51.160
They solve each case
with maximum violence.

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:55.720
These modern warriors are icons
of both order and terror.

00:03:55.880 --> 00:03:59.210
And working with these
brutal men is our subject:

00:03:59.210 --> 00:04:02.300
Patlabor pilot Noa Izumi.

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:06.310
Momoko Sakurayama will guide you
through this bizarre world!

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:09.610
The team members seem to be
gathered in here.

00:04:09.810 --> 00:04:11.610
Let's peek in, shall we?

00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:20.200
Now for the morning roll call.
Lt. Takeo Kumagami.

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:22.950
Officer Isao Ota.

00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:24.830
Officer Asuma Shinohara.

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:27.330
Officer Mikiyasu Shinshi.

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:29.840
Officer Hiromi Yamazaki.

00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:32.000
Officer Noa Izumi.

00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:38.670
All present.
Now, recite this week's resolution.

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:40.090
Always take care.

00:04:40.090 --> 00:04:46.180
If we should meet a rampaging
Labor in the dead of night, say...

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:48.150
May I butt in here?

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:51.900
Hey, aren't you
Momoko Sakurayama the TV star?

00:04:52.220 --> 00:04:55.270
Yes! I'm Momoko Sakurayama,
the action reporter!

00:04:55.270 --> 00:04:57.610
This is my director, Oguri,
and Inari on camera.

00:04:58.150 --> 00:05:05.830
For the next three days, we'd like to
document your life, Noa Izumi!

00:05:05.900 --> 00:05:07.910
It would be my pleasure.

00:05:07.910 --> 00:05:09.330
Cut!

00:05:09.740 --> 00:05:11.250
Cameraman, okay?

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:13.130
Momoko, okay?

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:15.330
Chief Fukushima, okay?

00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:17.630
Good, everything's okay.

00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:24.260
This piece will air next Wednesday.

00:05:24.550 --> 00:05:28.230
Momoko was very impressed
by the whole Plessie incident.

00:05:28.390 --> 00:05:32.560
She thought this would make
a good episode.

00:05:33.140 --> 00:05:38.200
It'll give the people of Tokyo
a chance to see the police at work.

00:05:38.230 --> 00:05:43.740
I'd be more than happy to explain
the administrative structure.

00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:46.240
Well, uh, gee, uh...

00:05:47.570 --> 00:05:50.030
I'd be <i>more than happy</i> to discuss it.

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:53.790
Yes, of course! Sometime.

00:05:57.460 --> 00:05:58.920
It makes you look fat.

00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:00.510
Really?

00:06:00.580 --> 00:06:03.180
They say the camera adds ten pounds.

00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:05.130
You should try fasting.

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:08.720
I think you should look natural,
Miss Izumi.

00:06:08.930 --> 00:06:10.440
I agree.

00:06:11.140 --> 00:06:14.650
Policemen don't need to be pretty,
they need to be brave!

00:06:14.810 --> 00:06:19.190
If good looks stopped criminals,
we'd report to Miss Universe!

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:24.990
I heard.

00:06:25.730 --> 00:06:28.580
Nice job, getting a documentary
on your team.

00:06:28.610 --> 00:06:30.250
It was the Chief's orders.

00:06:30.570 --> 00:06:33.130
It's hard to court the media.

00:06:33.620 --> 00:06:39.050
The Americans pick presidents
just because they're good on TV.

00:06:39.290 --> 00:06:40.760
Am I cut out for politics?

00:06:40.830 --> 00:06:43.340
Interested in running
for the House of Councilors?

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:47.560
Let us begin the courting!

00:06:54.010 --> 00:06:55.110
I lost.

00:06:55.810 --> 00:06:56.690
Next!

00:06:58.100 --> 00:06:59.150
I'm ready.

00:07:01.060 --> 00:07:02.520
Here in Special Vehicles,

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:07.410
no distinction is made between
men and women! Observe!

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:11.620
A storm blows today
through this jungle of mats!

00:07:18.410 --> 00:07:19.920
Next! Officer Izumi.

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:29.010
I'm ready.

00:07:49.570 --> 00:07:50.580
Cut!

00:07:51.610 --> 00:07:53.410
Hold that pose!

00:07:54.820 --> 00:07:58.740
Inari, can you get a shot
from over here?

00:07:59.120 --> 00:08:01.250
Great! Momoko, make up.
More sweat.

00:08:05.460 --> 00:08:07.050
Just a second.

00:08:11.510 --> 00:08:13.180
Ready.

00:08:18.760 --> 00:08:23.240
Okay, let's go. VTR's rolling. Action!

00:08:31.690 --> 00:08:32.790
Officer Izumi.

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:34.660
I'm fine.

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:42.330
Oh, you cut your cheek!
Are you all right, Miss Izumi?

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:43.620
Oh, it's nothing.

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:45.290
It's so realistic!

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:48.050
The beautiful Kumagami
throws plucky young Noa!

00:08:48.380 --> 00:08:49.720
Great stuff!

00:09:13.070 --> 00:09:14.080
Miss Izumi...

00:09:15.030 --> 00:09:19.830
I'm sorry about that.
Oguri has a big mouth, sometimes.

00:09:19.830 --> 00:09:22.380
That's okay. It doesn't bother me.

00:09:22.580 --> 00:09:29.090
Some girls have an inner beauty
that shines through in their work.

00:09:32.590 --> 00:09:35.850
Maybe you picked the wrong subject.

00:09:43.390 --> 00:09:45.530
Momoko, we're almost ready
for the live relay.

00:09:47.390 --> 00:09:50.070
Let's go. We can talk later.

00:09:51.610 --> 00:09:52.190
Sorry.

00:09:52.400 --> 00:09:53.950
You're late, Izumi.

00:09:54.110 --> 00:09:55.160
I'm sorry.

00:09:55.610 --> 00:09:58.410
This will be a live broadcast.
Noa, you stand in the middle.

00:10:00.070 --> 00:10:04.000
Chief Fukushima, don't force
yourself to smile. Act natural.

00:10:07.330 --> 00:10:10.330
Okay, we're ready.

00:10:10.330 --> 00:10:12.090
In three, two...

00:10:15.050 --> 00:10:15.840
Hello, everyone.

00:10:15.840 --> 00:10:22.850
The next episode of <i>The Working Girl</i>
will follow Miss Noa Izumi.

00:10:27.060 --> 00:10:29.820
I thought that was a boy!

00:10:36.030 --> 00:10:38.290
What's so funny, you idiots?

00:10:40.070 --> 00:10:43.410
Miss Izumi was the first
female police Labor pilot.

00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:45.840
She's solved dozens
of incredible cases!

00:10:46.330 --> 00:10:49.460
Tune in to see her excruciating life!

00:10:49.960 --> 00:10:52.430
Good work, people!

00:10:53.130 --> 00:10:58.770
Oops! Did I say excruciating?
I meant to say "exciting." Sorry!

00:11:00.010 --> 00:11:04.650
Well, that's live TV for you!
Noa, we'll get makeup to cover that.

00:11:07.270 --> 00:11:09.440
Okay, Noa? Okay.

00:11:27.450 --> 00:11:28.800
It's over.

00:11:51.980 --> 00:11:53.190
This way.

00:11:53.190 --> 00:11:55.110
Thanks for the help.

00:11:58.860 --> 00:12:01.450
Isn't this going too far?

00:12:01.740 --> 00:12:05.080
Hey, I'm trying for
total realism here.

00:12:05.820 --> 00:12:08.040
Is it okay to film her
while she sleeps?

00:12:08.910 --> 00:12:11.630
The public has a right to know!

00:12:11.910 --> 00:12:13.970
Couldn't this be dangerous?

00:12:14.790 --> 00:12:16.380
Ready to roll!

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:18.250
Start!

00:12:18.800 --> 00:12:22.680
And now, for our traditional
"peeking on sleeping" segment.

00:12:22.880 --> 00:12:27.310
It's four A.M., and Izumi is
just inside, sound asleep.

00:12:35.520 --> 00:12:40.620
Last week's model whispered
her lover's name in her sleep.

00:12:41.570 --> 00:12:43.410
Let's wake her up!

00:12:44.360 --> 00:12:48.290
Miss Izumi!
Miss Izumi, time to get up!

00:12:50.120 --> 00:12:52.050
Alphonse...

00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:53.960
He's a foreigner!

00:12:53.960 --> 00:12:55.840
That's the name of machine 1.

00:12:56.460 --> 00:13:00.800
It's morning!
Time to get up, Miss Izumi.

00:13:04.380 --> 00:13:07.690
I've got to make you pretty,
Alphonse.

00:13:07.840 --> 00:13:09.600
My makeup!

00:13:10.100 --> 00:13:11.350
Don't move.

00:13:11.350 --> 00:13:12.860
Miss Izumi!
Don't move.

00:13:12.970 --> 00:13:14.070
Cut!

00:13:15.520 --> 00:13:16.320
Huh?

00:13:16.730 --> 00:13:19.280
That was great, Noa! Fantastic!

00:13:21.860 --> 00:13:23.240
Oh no!

00:13:24.900 --> 00:13:27.540
I can't believe they all came in here!

00:13:33.830 --> 00:13:37.760
That was just so juvenile!

00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:44.090
Fine!

00:13:52.560 --> 00:13:53.860
What's that smell?

00:14:00.020 --> 00:14:03.940
So, Izumi, you finally decided
to look like a girl!

00:14:03.940 --> 00:14:05.440
You think I <i>don't</i>, usually?

00:14:05.440 --> 00:14:07.200
Clothes make the man.

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:08.290
Ota!

00:14:08.530 --> 00:14:10.170
You want to take me on?

00:14:15.540 --> 00:14:17.420
They did that to Izumi?

00:14:17.460 --> 00:14:20.380
Just so long as it doesn't
interfere with work.

00:14:20.380 --> 00:14:21.050
Sure.

00:14:21.540 --> 00:14:25.390
Oh no! I should have
put my money on 2-5.

00:14:25.800 --> 00:14:29.680
<i>505 in progress at the</i>
<i>Kawasaki Industrial Complex.</i>

00:14:33.310 --> 00:14:37.360
Division 2, 505 in Kawasaki.
Heading out to suppress it.

00:14:38.270 --> 00:14:39.900
Oh and...

00:14:45.570 --> 00:14:48.450
Listen to the next race.
I'll buy you dinner if I win.

00:14:49.240 --> 00:14:52.160
Gee, maybe I should just
broadcast it to you.

00:14:52.160 --> 00:14:54.040
You can be so stubborn.

00:14:55.580 --> 00:14:56.840
See you later!

00:14:59.710 --> 00:15:02.760
Bring the carrier out.
Prepare to load machine 1.

00:15:04.710 --> 00:15:05.300
Wait!

00:15:06.920 --> 00:15:08.600
Your cockpit feels hot.

00:15:08.760 --> 00:15:12.850
I don't want to point fingers,
but it smells like makeup.

00:15:12.970 --> 00:15:17.570
Don't let them pressure you
into doing something stupid.

00:15:18.140 --> 00:15:20.820
Thanks. I'll be okay.

00:15:24.060 --> 00:15:25.530
Don't dawdle.

00:15:28.610 --> 00:15:33.280
Hurry up! This is our scoop!
Realism awaits us in Kawasaki!

00:15:37.490 --> 00:15:38.250
Well?

00:15:38.330 --> 00:15:40.170
It looks like he's taking a break.

00:15:40.290 --> 00:15:45.470
What kind of idiot is he?
Who steals a Labor to commit suicide?

00:15:45.630 --> 00:15:50.510
Go away! I have a terminal disease!
Just leave me to die!

00:15:51.840 --> 00:15:54.770
Captain, how long are we
going to wait?

00:15:54.800 --> 00:15:57.230
<i>Kumagami is still running</i>
<i>a background check.</i>

00:15:57.600 --> 00:16:02.530
Get over it, bud. If you want to die,
jump off Mt. Fuji!

00:16:02.690 --> 00:16:04.650
That would be perfect
for a terminal disease.

00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:12.040
Halt!

00:16:20.250 --> 00:16:23.800
I'm standing exactly between
the criminal and Special Vehicles.

00:16:24.170 --> 00:16:29.720
What's the motive here?
And how will Noa Izumi handle it?

00:16:31.090 --> 00:16:33.180
And the big question is:

00:16:33.260 --> 00:16:37.150
What will the total cost
of damages be for this operation?

00:16:37.180 --> 00:16:41.650
For the exact price tag, stay tuned!

00:16:42.100 --> 00:16:45.150
Phones will close in five minutes.

00:16:45.190 --> 00:16:48.070
Calls will be answered in order.

00:16:48.440 --> 00:16:51.830
The first 20 callers will receive
a special phone card.

00:16:56.530 --> 00:16:57.290
Momoko!

00:16:57.820 --> 00:17:02.080
Your action reporter,
Momoko Sakurayama...

00:17:02.080 --> 00:17:07.800
has been captured by this hand of evil,
this modern King Kong!

00:17:08.080 --> 00:17:13.390
Farewell, viewers.
I may not be long for this world!

00:17:15.010 --> 00:17:16.100
Stay back!

00:17:16.720 --> 00:17:18.600
If you care about her...

00:17:18.600 --> 00:17:19.480
Momoko!

00:17:20.510 --> 00:17:21.860
Excuse me.

00:17:22.220 --> 00:17:23.690
Attention, criminal.

00:17:23.770 --> 00:17:26.820
Be careful not to kill your hostage.

00:17:26.900 --> 00:17:29.730
I'll take her with me to <i>hell!</i>

00:17:29.980 --> 00:17:32.370
But it's such a beautiful day.

00:17:32.480 --> 00:17:37.040
Life isn't that bad, you know.
Let's talk this over.

00:17:37.490 --> 00:17:39.160
Enough talk!

00:17:40.530 --> 00:17:41.630
Momoko!

00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:50.090
Dear viewers:
I don't think I'll last much longer.

00:17:50.500 --> 00:17:52.550
I'm glad you let me into your homes.

00:17:52.920 --> 00:17:57.350
I was... truly happy.

00:17:57.970 --> 00:18:03.520
Are you trying to make a fool of me?
Does this hurt?

00:18:03.520 --> 00:18:05.100
Do you understand how I feel?

00:18:05.100 --> 00:18:06.230
No, not really!

00:18:06.600 --> 00:18:09.570
You've got a lot of nerve!
<i>Now</i> you'll understand!

00:18:11.150 --> 00:18:14.360
Ow, ow! Hey, this really hurts!

00:18:14.570 --> 00:18:18.570
If you're going to kill me,
go ahead and get it over with!

00:18:18.570 --> 00:18:20.540
You are such a selfish brat!

00:18:22.030 --> 00:18:23.840
Looks like he'll be busy for a while.

00:18:24.330 --> 00:18:27.500
Captain, we've identified the criminal:

00:18:27.500 --> 00:18:31.380
Rudolf Shinbori, 21 years old,
known as "Fritter."

00:18:31.460 --> 00:18:32.970
What's he dying from?

00:18:33.290 --> 00:18:34.430
Well...

00:18:35.840 --> 00:18:37.270
Just a stomach ulcer?

00:18:37.760 --> 00:18:39.810
<i>He let his imagination run wild.</i>

00:18:40.340 --> 00:18:41.480
Geez.

00:18:47.230 --> 00:18:48.270
Shut up!

00:18:48.270 --> 00:18:49.520
You shut up!

00:18:49.520 --> 00:18:51.610
Mr. Sakaki was right.

00:18:54.020 --> 00:18:57.320
Hello, Mr. Shinbori?
Mr. Rudolf Shinbori?

00:18:57.320 --> 00:19:00.370
You snooped on me, didn't you?

00:19:00.530 --> 00:19:03.530
Yup, we got the full rundown.

00:19:04.620 --> 00:19:08.210
<i>For example,</i>
<i>we know about your stomach pains.</i>

00:19:08.500 --> 00:19:11.010
<i>Turns out it's just an ulcer.</i>

00:19:13.040 --> 00:19:20.350
What a cruel twist of fate!
Our criminal has a common complaint,

00:19:20.430 --> 00:19:24.260
one of the most popular sicknesses,
a stomach ulcer.

00:19:24.260 --> 00:19:26.890
Impossible! If it was just an ulcer,

00:19:26.890 --> 00:19:29.430
why didn't the doctors tell me?

00:19:30.060 --> 00:19:34.940
You don't have health insurance,
do you? They hate that.

00:19:34.940 --> 00:19:36.400
That's true...

00:19:36.400 --> 00:19:39.370
<i>Too soon, life turns to dust.</i>

00:19:39.490 --> 00:19:45.330
But can our culprit learn to live
with this crushing shame?

00:19:45.330 --> 00:19:46.120
What?

00:19:46.120 --> 00:19:48.160
Oh, I mean...

00:19:48.160 --> 00:19:50.880
One moment please. Yes? Yes?

00:19:51.460 --> 00:19:53.930
About that English phrase I just used...

00:19:53.960 --> 00:19:58.550
A professor in Itabashi just called in,
correcting me.

00:19:58.630 --> 00:20:00.800
Thank you, Professor in Itabashi.

00:20:00.800 --> 00:20:04.190
Shut up! What should I do now?

00:20:04.470 --> 00:20:07.230
Oh, this is being sent to
every station in the country.

00:20:07.890 --> 00:20:11.600
You'll be famous.
How embarrassing!

00:20:12.060 --> 00:20:13.320
You monster!

00:20:14.730 --> 00:20:18.870
Now you're really going to die!
I mean it!

00:20:19.030 --> 00:20:21.830
Back to the drawing board.

00:20:22.240 --> 00:20:24.370
I curse you all!

00:20:25.820 --> 00:20:27.290
You idiot!

00:20:27.370 --> 00:20:28.290
Momoko!

00:20:30.700 --> 00:20:31.700
I won't let you!

00:20:31.700 --> 00:20:33.340
Stay back, Izumi!

00:20:34.920 --> 00:20:35.930
Come back, Noa!

00:20:37.670 --> 00:20:41.100
This time, it's sayonara for sure!

00:20:43.840 --> 00:20:47.940
Momoko, you are more beautiful
than the wild chrysanthemum!

00:20:48.220 --> 00:20:49.480
Keep that camera rolling!

00:20:49.720 --> 00:20:52.020
Goodbye, everyone!

00:21:02.400 --> 00:21:03.490
I got him!

00:21:03.610 --> 00:21:05.000
Stay out of this!

00:21:06.410 --> 00:21:08.920
Goodbye, everyone!

00:21:09.780 --> 00:21:10.590
Damn!

00:21:28.090 --> 00:21:29.810
Momoko, are you okay?

00:21:30.720 --> 00:21:32.020
I'm okay.

00:21:44.940 --> 00:21:46.830
It'll be on in one minute!

00:21:47.490 --> 00:21:51.170
Yes, right now!
Your daddy's going to be on TV!

00:21:51.330 --> 00:21:55.050
Be sure to record it.
Call your mother to the TV.

00:21:57.170 --> 00:21:57.960
<i>...another glass!</i>

00:21:58.330 --> 00:22:00.430
Thanks for noting the positions.

00:22:00.460 --> 00:22:01.790
No problem.

00:22:01.790 --> 00:22:04.210
Are you talking about
horse racing again?

00:22:04.210 --> 00:22:08.680
Oh, yeah, I knew I'd heard
the criminal's name before!

00:22:08.720 --> 00:22:10.680
That happens all the time.

00:22:10.970 --> 00:22:14.400
Only ten seconds! Do something!

00:22:14.430 --> 00:22:16.480
Please don't hit me.

00:22:20.980 --> 00:22:22.030
Five seconds!

00:22:22.070 --> 00:22:22.730
Four,

00:22:22.940 --> 00:22:23.450
three,

00:22:23.820 --> 00:22:24.280
two,

00:22:24.730 --> 00:22:25.330
one,

00:22:25.530 --> 00:22:26.240
zero!

00:22:30.870 --> 00:22:34.710
The Working Girl<i>,</i>
<i>normally seen at this time,</i>

00:22:34.990 --> 00:22:37.760
<i>has been preempted this week</i>
<i>by the baseball playoffs.</i>

00:23:01.190 --> 00:23:06.490
arashi ga itsushika owatta
When I looked out, the storm had passed a long time ago.

00:23:07.280 --> 00:23:14.250
yuube no kobushi wa kirei ni
The morning dew betrays how yesterday's...

00:23:12.870 --> 00:23:16.120
arawareta
sorrows have been washed away.

00:23:16.120 --> 00:23:21.670
yoake ga NEJI wo yurumereba
Dawn is let loose by unbolting the panels of night.

00:23:22.250 --> 00:23:29.630
MASHIN ya BIRU ga mezameru
Even machines and the buildings all wake up.

00:23:29.630 --> 00:23:31.340
I got it

00:23:31.340 --> 00:23:38.890
tooku ga mieru yo PANORAMA mitai sa
Now I can see so far ahead, an unfolding panorama.

00:23:38.890 --> 00:23:44.770
doko kara mite mo heiwa-na Happy Island
Wherever I watch from, I see a peaceful, happy island.

00:23:44.770 --> 00:23:46.320
One more chance

00:23:46.320 --> 00:23:53.950
kimi ni oshietai kimi ni tsutaetai
The thing I want to tell to you, the thing I want to show to you

00:23:53.950 --> 00:23:59.870
yume no GEITO ga me no mae de
The shining gate to our dreams lays open to us...

00:23:59.870 --> 00:24:03.970
ima hiraku yo
right now before our eyes.

00:24:08.170 --> 00:24:13.300
This story is fiction...

00:24:08.170 --> 00:24:13.300
but in 10 years, who knows?

00:24:15.430 --> 00:24:20.690
The advancement of hypertechnology
led to the creation of Labors.

00:24:21.020 --> 00:24:26.610
But Labor crime becomes
a threat to society.

00:24:26.980 --> 00:24:32.330
The New York City police has created the
Crime Labor Attack Team as a response.

00:24:32.450 --> 00:24:35.080
And thus, CLAT was born.

00:24:35.200 --> 00:24:39.910
Next episode: Long Live CLAT.
Target, locked on!

00:24:39.200 --> 00:24:44.630
Next episode

00:24:39.200 --> 00:24:44.630
Long Live CLAT

00:24:39.910 --> 00:24:41.410
You took my line.
